<h2 style="font-size: 28px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Examination Overview - NISM Series I: Currency Derivatives Certification</h2>
<br />
										
                                        <div class="mb-2" style="color: #000;">
  <p>
    The examination aims to establish a standardized baseline of minimum knowledge for individuals operating within the currency derivative segment. The goal is to enhance comprehension of currency markets and exchange-traded currency derivative products, ultimately leading to improved quality in investor service, operational process efficiency, and strengthened risk controls.
  </p>

  <br />
<h2 style="font-size: 22px; color: #1565c0; margin-top: 30px;">Examination Objectives</h2>
<br />
  <ul class="car-single-list" style="color: #000;">
    <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i> Acquire a foundational understanding of currency markets, with a specific focus on Exchange Traded Currency Derivatives markets.</li>
    <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i> Comprehend the trading, clearing, and settlement mechanisms associated with Exchange Traded Currency Derivatives markets. Additionally, gain knowledge of basic investment strategies utilizing currency futures and options products.</li>
    <li><i class="far fa-check-circle"></i> Demonstrate knowledge of the regulatory environment governing exchange-traded currency Derivatives markets in India.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
<div style="border: 1px solid #90caf9; background-color: #e3f2fd; padding: 5px 8px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 20px 0;">
