    <div class="accordion-body" style="background-color: #e3f2fd; border-left: 5px solid #0d47a1; color: #000;">
      Once you pass the exam, the NISM Series I: Currency Derivatives Certification is valid for a period of three years. To keep your certification active after that, you will need to either re-take the exam or complete a Continuing Professional Education (CPE) program specified by NISM.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- FAQ 18 -->
<div class="accordion-item" style="border: 1px solid #1565c0; border-radius: 5px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
  <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading18">
    <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
            type="button"
            data-bs-toggle="collapse"
            data-bs-target="#collapse18"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="collapse18"
            style="background-color: #f1f8ff; font-weight: bold; color: #0D0D68; font-size: 16px;">
      18. Does your NISM I Practice Test include numerical questions?
    </button>
  </h2>
  <div id="collapse18" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading18" data-bs-parent="#faqCurrencyDerivatives">
    <div class="accordion-body" style="background-color: #e3f2fd; border-left: 5px solid #0d47a1; color: #000;">
      Yes, a good NISM I Practice Test must include numerical problems, as you can expect them in the actual exam. Our question bank includes practical, calculation-based questions related to topics like futures pricing, option payoffs, and margin calculations to ensure you are well-prepared for the quantitative aspects of the test.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- FAQ 19 -->
<div class="accordion-item" style="border: 1px solid #1565c0; border-radius: 5px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
  <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading19">
    <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
            type="button"
            data-bs-toggle="collapse"
            data-bs-target="#collapse19"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="collapse19"
            style="background-color: #f1f8ff; font-weight: bold; color: #0D0D68; font-size: 16px;">
      19. What is the difference between a Currency Derivatives Demo Test and a full mock test?
    </button>
  </h2>
  <div id="collapse19" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading19" data-bs-parent="#faqCurrencyDerivatives">
    <div class="accordion-body" style="background-color: #e3f2fd; border-left: 5px solid #0d47a1; color: #000;">
      A Currency Derivatives Demo Test is a short, free sample designed to give you a feel for the types of questions and the platform's interface. A full mock test, on the other hand, is a complete 100-question, 2-hour simulation of the actual exam, including the timer and negative marking. While a demo is good for a preview, only full mock tests can truly prepare you for the rigors of the exam.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- FAQ 20 -->
<div class="accordion-item" style="border: 1px solid #1565c0; border-radius: 5px; margin-bottom: 12px;">
  <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading20">
    <button class="accordion-button collapsed"
            type="button"
            data-bs-toggle="collapse"
            data-bs-target="#collapse20"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="collapse20"
            style="background-color: #f1f8ff; font-weight: bold; color: #0D0D68; font-size: 16px;">
      20. Why is understanding 'Clearing, Settlement & Risk Management' so important?
    </button>
  </h2>
  <div id="collapse20" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading20" data-bs-parent="#faqCurrencyDerivatives">
    <div class="accordion-body" style="background-color: #e3f2fd; border-left: 5px solid #0d47a1; color: #000;">
      This chapter has a significant 10% weightage because it covers the operational backbone of the derivatives market. It explains how trades are cleared, how profits and losses are settled daily (mark-to-market), and how the clearing corporation manages counterparty risk. A strong understanding of this is essential not just for the exam, but for anyone who wants to operate safely and effectively in the derivatives market.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

